# Review

The title makes a contestable claim about what a successful trial can establish and what recording the design rationale adds. An informed reader could argue that inspecting the boundaries and observing how they behave is enough to infer the conditions for reuse. The note argues that several reasons can explain the same working split, and that recording which constraint or requirement each boundary answered gives a reviewer a specific condition to check in a new context. The title's main predicate assigns that role to retained rationale, which is the substantive point under dispute.
